Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Like, a hundred tiny seeds blowing away through the air as the child

1208
01:47:08.090 --> 01:47:11.850
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Let's go of the hundred souls it held.

1209
01:47:12.080 --> 01:47:15.529
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And lets them send onward, and they flow.

1210
01:47:16.030 --> 01:47:17.040
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Straight.

1211
01:47:17.490 --> 01:47:28.049
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Swift in a direction away from every other direction, going to a home that none of you know, but to which you each will go one day, and they're gone.

1212
01:47:29.460 --> 01:47:30.080
Eric Rosenbaum: Hmm.

1213
01:47:35.180 --> 01:47:37.320
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Hanging in a makeshift backpack.

1214
01:47:37.660 --> 01:47:40.730
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): A ray opens its mouth and its eyes.

1215
01:47:41.630 --> 01:47:50.499
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): and says, What? Wha… wha-wh- And then its voice slows.

1216
01:47:50.910 --> 01:47:59.060
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And it goes still and inert, and you know that whatever powered it is gone, and in fact, whatever powered the whole of the 27th

1217
01:47:59.410 --> 01:48:00.360
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): room.

1218
01:48:00.870 --> 01:48:03.010
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): is… Gone.

1219
01:48:03.680 --> 01:48:05.060
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And the rumbling.

1220
01:48:05.210 --> 01:48:08.189
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Grows deeper, and at the same time.

1221
01:48:08.700 --> 01:48:13.270
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): The child begins to shift and change in its shape.

1222
01:48:14.190 --> 01:48:21.809
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And as the house collapses around you, it grows and bursts the prison open from the inside out.

1223
01:48:22.800 --> 01:48:26.899
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And this, what you see, you DO remember.

1224
01:48:27.020 --> 01:48:36.579
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): You remember, in every one of the worst moments of your life that come in all of the years that follow, this is what you see when you close your eyes. It is…

1225
01:48:36.800 --> 01:48:47.820
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): An un-thing. Made of bone and bramble and tree roots and mold, shaped something like a dandelion made of darkness seven stories tall.

1226
01:48:47.900 --> 01:49:03.540
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): In its roots, the size of elephants are alive and writhing like slugs, like pale leeches exposed to the light, terrified, unthinking, reaching through the boundaries of the multiverse like living and clawed things.

1227
01:49:04.270 --> 01:49:08.920
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And the dandelion at the top, this pale sphere, spread out.

1228
01:49:09.300 --> 01:49:26.040
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): At the end of each of those seeds are the faces of everyone you have ever met, trying to rip themselves free of the horror that they know that they are. A plant whose leaves around the base are tentacles of rot and bone and darkness, which, until recently.

1229
01:49:26.110 --> 01:49:34.300
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Wrapped themselves around the shimmering spheres of mortal souls which screamed for centuries without ever stopping.

1230
01:49:34.910 --> 01:49:36.410
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And what you know.

1231
01:49:36.600 --> 01:49:49.449
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): In the darkness and the nightmare moments in the decades to come are that this thing that you perceive is only the closest approximation your mind can make of what it actually is.

1232
01:49:51.480 --> 01:49:54.019
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And then it's a child again.

1233
01:49:55.370 --> 01:49:58.270
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And the ruins and remains of the prison.

1234
01:49:58.790 --> 01:50:06.259
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And of the house, now shaken apart around you as you were sheltered under one of these horror leaves.

1235
01:50:06.510 --> 01:50:12.760
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Are sliding down the sides of the cliff, and into the ravine, and into the darkness.

1236
01:50:14.630 --> 01:50:23.160
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): The child is sitting at the edge of a low stone well, maybe a foot high above the Cliffside.

1237
01:50:23.840 --> 01:50:28.040
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Where a doorframe used to be leading into the house.

1238
01:50:29.340 --> 01:50:33.810
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): It shakes the last of the milkweed puffs free from its hand.

1239
01:50:34.610 --> 01:50:37.620
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And looks at each of you simultaneously.

1240
01:50:38.310 --> 01:50:44.389
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And you see in it a child, and an adult, and a madman, and a monster, all at once.

1241
01:50:44.550 --> 01:50:47.760
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And it puts a single finger in front of its lips.

1242
01:50:48.310 --> 01:50:50.089
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And disappears down the well.

1243
01:50:51.630 --> 01:50:53.610
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And the five of you are left.

1244
01:50:54.180 --> 01:50:58.529
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): On an empty hillside, In the gathering twilight.

1245
01:50:59.000 --> 01:51:02.359
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Just as the first stars of evening are beginning to come out.

1246
01:51:11.820 --> 01:51:17.680
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): That's where we'll end, and I… I have a closing… Montage 2.

1247
01:51:18.370 --> 01:51:20.630
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): But before that, I want to give a moment, if there's…

1248
01:51:20.920 --> 01:51:27.790
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): conversation or business up among the five of you. I don't want to cut it off without… if there's anything that needs…

1249
01:51:28.160 --> 01:51:29.480
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Saying among the party.

1250
01:51:29.860 --> 01:51:31.369
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): But we are gonna leave you there.

1251
01:51:33.400 --> 01:51:34.909
Audio shared by David S. Kong: I don't think there's anything to say.

1252
01:51:44.720 --> 01:51:46.159
Eric Rosenbaum: Just so good.

1253
01:51:46.850 --> 01:51:48.229
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): I think from there…

1254
01:51:51.700 --> 01:51:55.210
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): The camera pans up and away from you.

1255
01:51:56.290 --> 01:51:59.820
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And out towards the horizon where the sun has set?

1256
01:52:01.620 --> 01:52:03.689
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And then pans back again.

1257
01:52:04.540 --> 01:52:10.500
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And it's the last of the sunset shining through a high window of an old house.

1258
01:52:10.670 --> 01:52:14.810
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Onto the bloody and exhausted form of Lord Hulda.

1259
01:52:15.210 --> 01:52:31.049
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Surrounded by the butchered corpse of the half-dozen mushroom men Aldens, who were his servants. And he drinks a potion, but his wounds don't fully close, and he coughs, and then he coughs again, and he doesn't stop coughing until he does, all at once.

1260
01:52:33.600 --> 01:52:39.079
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Below the old trees, on the wild edges of the Duchy of Tellim, it's always dusk.

1261
01:52:40.220 --> 01:52:53.960
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And in that twilight, the pale mushroom children of the thirst walk without sleeping or dreaming or hungering, and they flee from fire and iron, and they make new siblings out of anyone they find.

1262
01:52:54.980 --> 01:53:02.700
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And they search in those woods, always, obsessively, for the hidden door that will bring them back home to their parent again.

1263
01:53:06.110 --> 01:53:12.289
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): In a room filled with glass tanks of fungus, Growing on severed limbs.

1264
01:53:13.960 --> 01:53:18.949
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Just as you feel the first rumbles start to vibrate.

1265
01:53:19.090 --> 01:53:25.090
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Through, just as you can see the glass tanks shaking and the houses destroyed.

1266
01:53:26.020 --> 01:53:40.799
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): A body in the shape of a dwarven woman, but made from fungi and lichens of every possible description, sits up and looks, for a long moment, at the lifeless corpse which once held the soul now encased in its own fungal golem flesh.

1267
01:53:41.940 --> 01:53:57.510
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And as the room around her shakes, as pieces of the ceiling begin to fall to the floor, Calypses, now wizard head of Erythramos lamparum in a golem body, consults a book filled with long lists of six-digit numbers and blinks out of sight.

1268
01:54:01.030 --> 01:54:02.520
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): Camera pulls back.

1269
01:54:03.280 --> 01:54:17.880
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And it's a quiet, thatched cottage by the side of a road which runs parallel exactly to the sunset, and a tigerman is stowing in his bag the polished sphere of crystal through which he watched a golem plane shift out of the Feywild.

1270
01:54:18.560 --> 01:54:21.390
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And he draws thoughtfully from his pipe.

1271
01:54:22.140 --> 01:54:23.600
Audio shared by David S. Kong: and size.

1272
01:54:23.760 --> 01:54:29.840
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): And at the corners of his mouth, a sly smile creeps across the massive tiger face.

1273
01:54:33.330 --> 01:54:48.159
Rev. David Schwartz (he/him): It is no time. It is not time, it is outside of time, in the black nothingness beyond the universe, where the black stars do not shine, and an un-thing that is sometimes a child, and sometimes a monster.

1274
01:54:48.160 --> 01:54:59.999
